- Removed the deprecated `/api/v1/fleet/mdm/...` aliases of endpoints that moved out of `/mdm`, such as `/mdm/commands`, `/mdm/profiles`, `/mdm/bootstrap`, and `/mdm/setup/eula`, and the deprecated `/mdm/apple/profiles`, `/mdm/apple/commands`, `/mdm/apple/filevault/summary`, `PATCH /mdm/apple/settings`, `POST /mdm/apple/request_csr`, and `POST /mdm/apple/dep/key_pair` endpoints. They now return 410 with a link to the Fleet 5 migration guide.
- Fleet now sends hosts the bootstrap package URL `/api/latest/fleet/bootstrap?token=`. `GET /api/latest/fleet/mdm/bootstrap?token=` still works for hosts that were sent the old URL. If you limit which Fleet paths are reachable from the internet, allow `/api/*/fleet/bootstrap` and `/api/*/fleet/setup_experience/eula/*`.
- The API-only user form no longer sends grants for endpoints that are no longer in the API endpoint catalog.
- `fleetctl` now uses the current endpoints. Upgrade `fleetctl` together with the Fleet server: older versions of `fleetctl gitops` (with `bootstrap_package`), `fleetctl get mdm-apple`, `fleetctl mdm run-command`, and `fleetctl generate-gitops` call removed endpoints.
